WEBVTT


00:01:43.625 --> 00:01:46.348
Happy Thanksgiving!


00:01:53.675 --> 00:01:55.595
- Here!
- Right here!


00:02:01.003 --> 00:02:02.923
Here you go, fellas!


00:02:10.052 --> 00:02:11.972
Come! Come here.


00:02:24.867 --> 00:02:26.787
This is the problem.


00:02:27.069 --> 00:02:29.702
This is what's wrong with America.


00:02:29.712 --> 00:02:31.344
It's gotten so big


00:02:31.353 --> 00:02:33.720
you just can't find your way.


00:02:33.836 --> 00:02:35.307
The grocery store


00:02:35.317 --> 00:02:37.630
on the corner is a now a supermarket.


00:02:37.639 --> 00:02:39.351
The candy store


00:02:39.361 --> 00:02:41.281
is a MacDonald's.


00:02:42.044 --> 00:02:43.796
And this place...


00:02:43.805 --> 00:02:46.198
a super fucking discount store.


00:02:46.207 --> 00:02:48.737
Where's the pride of ownership?


00:02:50.331 --> 00:02:52.698
Where's the personal service?


00:02:59.181 --> 00:03:00.652
See what I mean?


00:03:00.662 --> 00:03:02.582
Shit...


00:03:03.985 --> 00:03:05.818
What right do they have


00:03:05.828 --> 00:03:08.140
of cutting out the suppliers?


00:03:08.150 --> 00:03:10.598
Pushing out all the middlemen.


00:03:11.833 --> 00:03:14.771
Buying direct from the manufacturer.


00:03:16.198 --> 00:03:17.829
Sony this.


00:03:17.839 --> 00:03:19.759
Toshiba that.


00:03:19.841 --> 00:03:21.757
All them Chinks...


00:03:21.766 --> 00:03:23.884
put Americans out of work.


00:03:23.925 --> 00:03:27.039
<i>...plans to take place
in Quang Tri Province.</i>


00:03:27.048 --> 00:03:28.968
<i>From Laos...</i>


00:03:30.692 --> 00:03:32.732
That's the way it is now.


00:03:35.777 --> 00:03:37.697
You're all right?


00:03:37.779 --> 00:03:40.962
You can't find the heart of anything...


00:03:42.023 --> 00:03:43.943
to stick the knife.


00:03:47.708 --> 00:03:49.628
Anybody here?


00:03:50.152 --> 00:03:52.344
- Can I help you?
- Call an ambulance.


00:03:52.354 --> 00:03:54.274
Forget it, Frank.


00:03:55.717 --> 00:03:57.757
There's no one in charge.


00:04:02.524 --> 00:04:04.444
Call an ambulance!


00:04:05.247 --> 00:04:07.720
<i>Some say Bumpy Johnson
was a great man,</i>


00:04:07.729 --> 00:04:09.881
<i>according to eulogies,
a giving man.</i>


00:04:09.891 --> 00:04:12.124
<i>A man of the people.
No one chose to use</i>


00:04:12.134 --> 00:04:14.486
<i>in remembrances
the word most often associated</i>


00:04:14.495 --> 00:04:16.848
<i>with Ellsworth Bumpy Johnson:
Gangster,</i>


00:04:16.858 --> 00:04:19.290
<i>whose passing has brought
a Who's Who of mourners</i>


00:04:19.300 --> 00:04:20.652
<i>on this chilly afternoon.</i>


00:04:20.661 --> 00:04:22.815
<i>The KC mob boss,
Dominic Cattano.</i>


00:04:22.824 --> 00:04:25.456
<i>Harlem crime figure,
Nicky Barnes.</i>


00:04:25.466 --> 00:04:26.978
<i>From the political arena,</i>


00:04:26.988 --> 00:04:29.261
<i>the Governor has come down.
The Mayor of New York,</i>


00:04:29.270 --> 00:04:31.142
<i>the Chief of Police and Commissioner.</i>


00:04:31.152 --> 00:04:33.785
<i>Sports and entertainment luminaries.</i>


00:04:33.795 --> 00:04:36.508
<i>Bumpy Johnson,
age 62 when he passed</i>


00:04:36.517 --> 00:04:40.272
<i>was a folk hero among Harlem locals
for over four decades.</i>


00:04:40.282 --> 00:04:42.714
<i>Regarded by some as
the Robin Hood of Harlem,</i>


00:04:42.724 --> 00:04:45.417
<i>by others as a ruthless criminal.</i>


00:04:46.287 --> 00:04:50.442
I would've thought that Warnfield
put out a better spread.


00:04:50.452 --> 00:04:52.492
- Want some?
- No, thanks.


00:04:52.813 --> 00:04:55.180
I want chicken wings on mine.


00:04:55.216 --> 00:04:56.568
Who is that?


00:04:56.578 --> 00:04:58.330
He didn't know what hit him.


00:04:58.339 --> 00:05:01.195
I just kept poppin'
him in the face.


00:05:06.988 --> 00:05:08.908
You got a light?


00:05:20.961 --> 00:05:22.881
That's very good.


00:05:22.924 --> 00:05:24.844
Hey, Frank!


00:05:26.247 --> 00:05:29.022
Get me a light while you're at it.


00:05:30.331 --> 00:05:32.251
Appreciate it.


00:05:32.734 --> 00:05:34.165
Don Cattano.


00:05:34.175 --> 00:05:36.095
How you doing, Rossi?


00:05:37.218 --> 00:05:38.770
- Good.
- A drink, Sir?


00:05:38.780 --> 00:05:40.700
Give him a scotch.


00:05:46.147 --> 00:05:48.067
Come on.


00:05:57.238 --> 00:05:59.604
I know you're hurting, Frank.


00:05:59.800 --> 00:06:01.513
So am I.


00:06:01.522 --> 00:06:03.195
I'm all right.


00:06:03.204 --> 00:06:05.517
- You going to be all right?
- Yeah.


00:06:05.526 --> 00:06:07.999
I'm sure Bumpy didn't tell you,
but he made me promise


00:06:08.009 --> 00:06:10.241
if anything happened to him...


00:06:10.251 --> 00:06:11.563
I should make sure


00:06:11.572 --> 00:06:13.939
that you're want for nothing.


00:06:14.575 --> 00:06:16.495
I appreciate that.


00:06:16.737 --> 00:06:20.331
Half the people here
owed Bumpy money when he died.


00:06:20.341 --> 00:06:23.694
They think I'll forget to collect,
but I'll get that money.


00:06:23.704 --> 00:06:25.826
Well... that's the spirit.


00:06:25.906 --> 00:06:27.826
Go get them.


00:06:29.670 --> 00:06:31.542
<i>Mr. Roberts!</i>


00:06:31.552 --> 00:06:33.265
Taking the prosecution side,


00:06:33.274 --> 00:06:34.786
give us U.S. vs. Meade,


00:06:34.796 --> 00:06:37.468
subject, issues,
what the determination was


00:06:37.478 --> 00:06:39.926
and what it means to us today.


00:06:40.201 --> 00:06:41.913
Class shall be critiquing,


00:06:41.923 --> 00:06:44.371
Mr. Roberts, so pay attention.


00:06:46.567 --> 00:06:48.840
<i>I hate hearing my name,
ya know?</i>


00:06:48.849 --> 00:06:50.721
Means I gotta get up
in front of the class,


00:06:50.731 --> 00:06:53.644
I gotta turn around,
and I know everyone in there,


00:06:53.654 --> 00:06:55.694
they know more than I do.


00:06:55.816 --> 00:06:57.448
The N°1 fear of people...


00:06:57.457 --> 00:06:59.530
it ain't dying.
It's public speaking.


00:06:59.540 --> 00:07:01.292
I get physically ill.
Wanna throw up.


00:07:01.301 --> 00:07:02.974
And you wanna do that
for a living.


00:07:02.983 --> 00:07:05.135
I don't like being like that.
I want to beat it.


00:07:05.145 --> 00:07:07.338
- Should I do this?
- No, he'll take it from me.


00:07:07.347 --> 00:07:08.820
He knows me since high school.


00:07:08.830 --> 00:07:10.781
- High school?
- Good morning.


00:07:10.791 --> 00:07:12.743
He doesn't take it, just throw it in.


00:07:12.753 --> 00:07:15.691
- That's good service.
- Throw it in?


00:07:16.637 --> 00:07:18.549
- What's up, Suzie?
- Hi, Jay.


00:07:18.559 --> 00:07:21.333
- How you doing, baby?
- All right.


00:07:45.546 --> 00:07:47.466
You, punk!


00:07:48.148 --> 00:07:50.551
You bit me, asshole!


00:07:51.792 --> 00:07:54.785
I swear to God, Richie.
I didn't know it was you.


00:07:54.795 --> 00:07:57.308
I'd never slam a door
on your hand, knowingly.


00:07:57.318 --> 00:07:58.589
You bit my fucking hand.


00:07:58.599 --> 00:08:00.391
What you doing
serving subpoenas anyway?


00:08:00.401 --> 00:08:02.513
- We're on loan to County.
- County?


00:08:02.523 --> 00:08:05.035
- How's that working for you?
- Fuck you.


00:08:05.045 --> 00:08:07.158
I'm sorry.
Consider me served.


00:08:07.168 --> 00:08:08.599
Can we leave it there?


00:08:08.608 --> 00:08:10.521
Assault on a police officer?


00:08:10.530 --> 00:08:11.963
I don't think so.


00:08:11.972 --> 00:08:15.246
For old time's sake, what can we do,
what do you want, what can I give you?


00:08:15.255 --> 00:08:17.488
What do you get for assault
with a deadly weapon, Jay?


00:08:17.498 --> 00:08:19.490
- 5 years minimum.
- 5 years.


00:08:19.500 --> 00:08:21.420
Guys, c'mon! No.


00:08:21.542 --> 00:08:23.494
Guys, what do you want?
Who do you want?


00:08:23.504 --> 00:08:25.136
- Who do you got?
- You want...


00:08:25.145 --> 00:08:27.757
Big Al's bookie, his accountant?


00:08:27.988 --> 00:08:29.908
I'll give him to you.


00:08:37.717 --> 00:08:39.637
Stop, stop.


00:08:40.200 --> 00:08:42.120
There he is.


00:08:44.124 --> 00:08:46.044
That's him. The bookie.


00:08:46.366 --> 00:08:47.758
All right. Get lost.


00:08:47.768 --> 00:08:50.161
- Right here?
- Right here. Get out of the car.


00:08:50.171 --> 00:08:51.562
- This is nuts.
- Come on.


00:08:51.571 --> 00:08:53.444
Let's go.


00:08:53.454 --> 00:08:55.374
Take it easy.


00:09:14.114 --> 00:09:15.906
We stay with him or the car?


00:09:15.916 --> 00:09:18.527
Let's see who comes for the car.


00:09:32.252 --> 00:09:34.172
Think he made us?


00:09:34.334 --> 00:09:36.847
You called in a warrant, right?
So where are they?


00:09:36.857 --> 00:09:38.569
I just called, man!


00:09:38.578 --> 00:09:43.311
I called and walked back here,
and ten seconds has gone by.


00:09:44.424 --> 00:09:46.297
We saw him with the slips, Jay.


00:09:46.306 --> 00:09:48.779
You saw policy slips?
You saw grocery bags.


00:09:48.789 --> 00:09:51.061
- You don't know what's in them.
- I do, and so do you.


00:09:51.071 --> 00:09:52.463
Don't give me that bull.


00:09:52.472 --> 00:09:53.824
What's the rush, Richie?


00:09:53.834 --> 00:09:56.187
- Half an hour, the warrant'll be here.
- I got night school.


00:09:56.196 --> 00:09:58.399
Guess you're gonna miss it.


00:10:06.166 --> 00:10:08.118
- Fuck this. Come on!
- You sure?


00:10:08.128 --> 00:10:10.048
Yeah, let's go.


00:11:00.861 --> 00:11:02.781
Fuck!


00:11:11.391 --> 00:11:13.311
Fuck!


00:11:35.815 --> 00:11:39.690
- It's not just a couple of bucks.
- It's the same thing, in principle.


00:11:39.699 --> 00:11:41.491
We're talking principles?


00:11:41.501 --> 00:11:43.733
A cop who turns in
this kind of money...


00:11:43.743 --> 00:11:47.137
says one thing.
He turns in cops who take money.


00:11:47.147 --> 00:11:49.779
- We'll be fucking pariahs.
- We're fucked both ways.


00:11:49.789 --> 00:11:52.662
Not if we keep it. Only if we don't,
then right, we're fucked,


00:11:52.672 --> 00:11:54.592
but not if we keep it.


00:11:55.314 --> 00:11:56.987
Goddamn it, man!


00:11:56.996 --> 00:11:59.189
Did we ask for it?
Did we put a gun to someone's head


00:11:59.199 --> 00:12:00.790
and say: "Give us your money"?


00:12:00.800 --> 00:12:02.962
Cops... kill cops


00:12:03.282 --> 00:12:05.202
they can't trust.


00:12:07.847 --> 00:12:09.887
We can't turn it in, man.


00:12:18.658 --> 00:12:20.578
You believe that?


00:12:28.948 --> 00:12:30.868
How much is there?


00:12:31.150 --> 00:12:34.251
Nine hundred
and eighty seven thousand.


00:12:35.315 --> 00:12:37.436
What happened to the rest?


00:12:39.919 --> 00:12:44.675
What the hell are you doing counting it
in front of everybody. Are you nuts?


00:12:44.684 --> 00:12:50.396
Get it back in the bags, seal 'em up,
and down it to the property room.


00:12:58.177 --> 00:13:00.097
Fucking boy-scouts.


00:13:11.350 --> 00:13:14.369
So nice to see you here this evening.


00:13:22.881 --> 00:13:24.801
What?


00:13:24.844 --> 00:13:26.764
What?


00:13:48.707 --> 00:13:50.829
Detective Trupo.
Sign here.


00:13:54.914 --> 00:13:57.027
You guys ready
to make a lot of fuckin' money?


00:13:57.036 --> 00:13:58.956
- Always.
- Hell yeah.


00:14:02.762 --> 00:14:04.473
Here you go!


00:14:04.483 --> 00:14:06.235
All right. Look at this.


00:14:06.244 --> 00:14:09.835
- Fucking dealers.
- Here's three more boats.


00:14:16.375 --> 00:14:18.487
Hey, don't lose any of that shit.


00:14:18.497 --> 00:14:20.417
- I know.
- Be careful.


00:14:24.423 --> 00:14:27.116
Just enough for the reagent test.


00:14:27.746 --> 00:14:29.666
A little less.


00:14:34.794 --> 00:14:37.146
<i>This is the French Connection dope.</i>


00:14:37.155 --> 00:14:41.471
<i>Kilos of the same dope Eddie Egan
and Sonny Grasso took from us!</i>


00:14:41.480 --> 00:14:43.752
<i>The cops seize it, arrest everyone,</i>


00:14:43.762 --> 00:14:46.155
<i>and they start taking it out
of the evidence room,</i>


00:14:46.165 --> 00:14:49.599
<i>whacking it down to nothing
and selling it back to us.</i>


00:14:49.608 --> 00:14:52.001
<i>They basically
control the market with it.</i>


00:14:52.010 --> 00:14:53.930
Mr. Rossi.
A surprise.


00:14:54.052 --> 00:14:56.686
<i>They've been doin' this for years.
They live off it.</i>


00:14:56.695 --> 00:14:58.447
<i>- Our dope.
- Many thanks.</i>


00:14:58.457 --> 00:15:00.970
What the fuck is happening
to the world, Frank?


00:15:00.980 --> 00:15:02.900
Fuckin' crooks.


00:15:03.582 --> 00:15:05.502
Sad about Bumpy.


00:15:07.186 --> 00:15:09.458
Things are never gonna be the same
in Harlem.


00:15:09.468 --> 00:15:11.060
You walk down the street.


00:15:11.069 --> 00:15:14.423
Nobody bothers you
cause Bumpy was making sure of it.


00:15:14.433 --> 00:15:16.349
Here, Frankie.


00:15:16.359 --> 00:15:18.275
How is it there now?


00:15:18.757 --> 00:15:21.776
It's chaos.
Every gorilla for himself.


00:15:27.686 --> 00:15:29.606
Who can live like that?


00:15:29.768 --> 00:15:31.520
There has to be order.


00:15:31.530 --> 00:15:33.643
That would've never happened
with Italians.


00:15:33.652 --> 00:15:36.325
More important than
any one man's life...


00:15:36.334 --> 00:15:38.254
is order.


00:15:44.944 --> 00:15:46.864
Frank.


00:15:48.467 --> 00:15:50.387
Come on in.
Sit down.


00:15:54.753 --> 00:15:56.465
- How y'all doin'?
- Good.


00:15:56.475 --> 00:15:59.228
- So, you seen Nate over there?
- Yeah, all the time.


00:15:59.238 --> 00:16:00.509
Nate is everywhere.


00:16:00.519 --> 00:16:02.231
- He's good.
- He's still over there.


00:16:02.241 --> 00:16:04.072
Got himself a club now.


00:16:04.082 --> 00:16:05.394
Where, Saigon?


00:16:05.404 --> 00:16:06.636
Bangkok.


00:16:06.645 --> 00:16:09.583
I don't think he's ever comin' home.


00:16:12.931 --> 00:16:14.851
Come on.


00:16:39.637 --> 00:16:42.471
On the house
for our boys in uniform.


00:16:42.481 --> 00:16:45.255
Thank you, sugar,
that's very kind.


00:16:45.844 --> 00:16:47.075
Thank Frank.


00:16:47.085 --> 00:16:49.005
Thanks, Frank.


00:16:49.968 --> 00:16:51.888
Just relax.


00:16:52.290 --> 00:16:56.045
You gonna have to boot this,
shoot a couple times.


00:16:56.054 --> 00:16:57.847
Cops keep cutting it.


00:16:57.856 --> 00:16:59.776
Selling the shit.


00:17:01.459 --> 00:17:04.573
I won't say anything
cause the price is right.


00:17:04.583 --> 00:17:06.295
But that shit in Nam


00:17:06.304 --> 00:17:08.224
is way...


00:17:08.506 --> 00:17:10.018
way...


00:17:10.028 --> 00:17:11.948
heavy...


00:17:34.933 --> 00:17:37.381
Didn't you see the jar, Frank?


00:17:37.975 --> 00:17:40.668
I think you walked right past it.


00:17:40.899 --> 00:17:42.851
The money jar.
What I gotta do?


00:17:42.861 --> 00:17:44.901
Put a fuckin' sign on it?


00:17:48.987 --> 00:17:51.059
What are you thinking?
You know,


00:17:51.069 --> 00:17:53.221
Bumpy don't own 116th no more.


00:17:53.231 --> 00:17:55.944
He don't own no real estate
in Harlem right now. I'm the landlord,


00:17:55.953 --> 00:17:57.873
and the lease is 20%.


00:17:59.237 --> 00:18:01.790
Well, don't sell dope then, Frank.


00:18:01.800 --> 00:18:04.472
Get a real job.
Need a fuckin' job, Frank?


00:18:04.482 --> 00:18:07.155
Is that what you need?
You come work for me.


00:18:07.165 --> 00:18:10.358
You can drive me around.
You open my doors.


00:18:10.368 --> 00:18:15.753
Yes sir, no sir, right away sir.
Anything you want, Master Johnson.


00:18:17.295 --> 00:18:19.215
20%.


00:18:25.543 --> 00:18:27.502
20% is my profit, Tango.


00:18:30.068 --> 00:18:32.060
I give you that, what do I got left?
Nothing.


00:18:32.069 --> 00:18:35.824
20% puts me and everyone you know
out of business.


00:18:35.833 --> 00:18:37.866
There are legitimate ways
of doing things,


00:18:37.875 --> 00:18:41.149
and there's this way.
Not even Bumpy took 20%.


00:18:41.159 --> 00:18:43.079
Bumpy's fuckin' dead.


00:18:46.124 --> 00:18:47.835
My man.


00:18:47.845 --> 00:18:49.765
20%?


00:18:57.495 --> 00:18:59.207
20%.


00:18:59.217 --> 00:19:01.137
Doc! Let's go.


00:19:03.381 --> 00:19:05.853
<i>The drug problem in Vietnam
is more</i>


00:19:05.863 --> 00:19:07.696
<i>than marijuana.
At this point,</i>


00:19:07.705 --> 00:19:11.339
<i>it is estimated that one third
of American troops are experimenting</i>


00:19:11.349 --> 00:19:13.268
<i>with opium and heroin.</i>


00:19:13.751 --> 00:19:15.664
<i>The authorities say they've confiscated</i>


00:19:15.673 --> 00:19:19.388
<i>large quantities of marijuana,
heroin, and pills.</i>


00:19:19.397 --> 00:19:22.190
<i>Every person and every vehicle
going through the gates</i>


00:19:22.199 --> 00:19:24.392
<i>is subject to a thorough shakedown.</i>


00:19:24.402 --> 00:19:26.194
<i>Soldiers have access to the drugs</i>


00:19:26.203 --> 00:19:30.438
<i>at many rest and relaxation spots
in Bangkok, Saigon, and other areas</i>


00:19:30.448 --> 00:19:32.280
<i>throughout Vietnam and Thailand.</i>


00:19:32.290 --> 00:19:34.562
<i>Officials say the easy availability</i>


00:19:34.572 --> 00:19:37.806
<i>of relatively cheap cost
of high purity heroin</i>


00:19:37.816 --> 00:19:39.928
<i>throughout Saigon and the Far East</i>


00:19:39.937 --> 00:19:42.290
<i>is leading to an epidemic
of heroin addiction</i>


00:19:42.300 --> 00:19:44.220
<i>among U.S. soldiers.</i>


00:19:47.505 --> 00:19:49.377
<i>- Operator.
- Yeah, international.</i>


00:19:49.386 --> 00:19:51.389
<i>- What city?
- Bangkok.</i>


00:19:51.548 --> 00:19:52.901
<i>You know the country code?</i>


00:19:52.911 --> 00:19:54.663
Yeah, 376.


00:19:54.672 --> 00:19:59.242
<i>- For the first 3 minutes, it'll...
- I got it, I got it.</i>


00:20:02.720 --> 00:20:04.191
<i>- Sawadeekap.
- Hello?</i>


00:20:04.201 --> 00:20:05.993
<i>"Soul brothers".
Can I help you?</i>


00:20:06.003 --> 00:20:07.475
Nate!


00:20:07.484 --> 00:20:09.557
<i>- Do I know you?
- It's me.</i>


00:20:09.567 --> 00:20:12.667
<i>- Who?
- Me, Frank! Your cousin, negro.</i>


00:20:16.133 --> 00:20:18.336
Go get yourself a new suit.


00:20:53.370 --> 00:20:54.802
Look, I'm sorry.


00:20:54.812 --> 00:20:56.564
Please, Richie.


00:20:56.574 --> 00:21:00.128
Couldn't be avoided.
I'll take him next weekend, OK?


00:21:00.137 --> 00:21:01.689
We're moving.


00:21:01.699 --> 00:21:03.619
What? Where?


00:21:05.022 --> 00:21:07.551
The St. Regis.
What do you care?


00:21:09.706 --> 00:21:11.178
My sister's.


00:21:11.188 --> 00:21:13.146
Your sister's. In Vegas?


00:21:13.190 --> 00:21:15.223
- Yeah.
- You're not moving to Las Vegas.


00:21:15.232 --> 00:21:17.024
Not with Michael.


00:21:17.034 --> 00:21:19.787
What am I supposed to do with him?
Leave him with you?


00:21:19.797 --> 00:21:21.669
There's a picture.


00:21:21.679 --> 00:21:23.599
Hey, guys!
Be cool.


00:21:25.803 --> 00:21:27.235
Laurie, Las Vegas


00:21:27.245 --> 00:21:29.196
is not the kind of place
to raise a kid.


00:21:29.206 --> 00:21:31.118
Oh, like this is a good environment?


00:21:31.128 --> 00:21:32.440
And around your friends?


00:21:32.450 --> 00:21:34.322
When am I supposed to see my boy?


00:21:34.331 --> 00:21:36.534
This weekend, last weekend.


00:21:40.418 --> 00:21:42.129
I asked you nice to shut up, right?


00:21:42.139 --> 00:21:43.972
Now I'll have to kill you.
I swear


00:21:43.981 --> 00:21:46.414
I'll pull out my gun
and put a bullet in your fuckin' head!


00:21:46.423 --> 00:21:48.496
Stop what you're doin',
and pick up the glass!


00:21:48.506 --> 00:21:50.464
Calm down, man. Be cool.


00:21:53.550 --> 00:21:55.470
He's fuckin' crazy.


00:21:56.073 --> 00:21:57.993
You don't have a gun.


00:22:00.437 --> 00:22:02.357
You sure?


00:22:09.647 --> 00:22:11.567
You're crazy, Richie.


00:22:15.332 --> 00:22:17.535
You don't have room for us.


00:22:19.096 --> 00:22:21.016
I'll see you in court.


00:22:22.419 --> 00:22:24.339
Come on, Michael!


00:22:24.421 --> 00:22:26.341
Say bye to your dad.


00:22:27.144 --> 00:22:29.064
Hey, kiddo!


00:22:30.627 --> 00:22:33.647
See you next week.
We'll do something.


00:22:34.671 --> 00:22:36.874
Let's get you an ice cream.


00:23:00.497 --> 00:23:02.945
<i>You have 10 minutes remaining.</i>


00:23:03.219 --> 00:23:05.139
10 minutes.


00:24:15.132 --> 00:24:18.559
Girl, don't talk.
I wanna do a little funk.


00:24:54.210 --> 00:24:56.130
How much you want?


00:24:56.933 --> 00:24:59.136
Tell him I want a 100 ki's.


00:25:01.057 --> 00:25:03.089
Ain't nobody I know
who can get you that much.


00:25:03.099 --> 00:25:05.332
You have to piece it together
from different sources.


00:25:05.341 --> 00:25:07.774
And it's not gonna be 100% pure.


00:25:07.784 --> 00:25:09.296
I don't want that.


00:25:09.305 --> 00:25:10.977
I know what you don't want.


00:25:10.987 --> 00:25:15.622
But you'll need to get
to the Chi-Chou syndicate, all right?


00:25:15.632 --> 00:25:18.064
In Cholon, Saigon.
If they'll deal with you at all.


00:25:18.074 --> 00:25:20.547
I understand, but
by then, it'll be too late.


00:25:20.556 --> 00:25:23.149
It'll be already chopped up.
I want to get it where they get it from.


00:25:23.159 --> 00:25:24.391
The source.


00:25:24.400 --> 00:25:27.011
- And get it yourself?
- Why not?


00:25:28.364 --> 00:25:30.156
I came this far.


00:25:30.166 --> 00:25:32.879
- You'd go into the motherfuckin' jungle?
- I'm in it. Look around,


00:25:32.888 --> 00:25:34.881
They're eating these roaches,
whatever that is.


00:25:34.891 --> 00:25:36.643
Nigga, I'm talking about snakes.


00:25:36.653 --> 00:25:41.549
Tigers, Viet Congs, mosquitoes
that'll fuckin' kill your ass.


00:25:43.099 --> 00:25:46.771
- You wanna go into the jungle?
- We're going.


00:25:47.703 --> 00:25:49.336
- Fuck it, let's go.
- We're going.


00:25:49.346 --> 00:25:51.266
Why not?


00:26:31.587 --> 00:26:33.507
Hey, Frank.


00:26:33.790 --> 00:26:37.625
This whole spot's locked down
by the Kuomintang.


00:26:38.233 --> 00:26:41.334
General Chang Kai Chek's
defeated army.


00:27:17.754 --> 00:27:20.066
How would you get it into the States?


00:27:20.076 --> 00:27:21.948
You ain't got to worry about that.


00:27:21.957 --> 00:27:25.631
- Who do you work for in there?
- Don't worry about that either.


00:27:25.641 --> 00:27:27.561
Who are you really?


00:27:27.883 --> 00:27:30.036
Frank Lucas,
like it says on my passport.


00:27:30.045 --> 00:27:32.738
- I mean, who you represent?
- Me.


00:27:34.970 --> 00:27:38.644
You think you're going to take
a 100 kilos of heroin into the U.S.


00:27:38.654 --> 00:27:42.729
and you don't work for anyone?
Someone's going to allow that?


00:27:42.738 --> 00:27:44.658
That's right.


00:27:50.826 --> 00:27:53.111
After this first purchase...


00:27:53.348 --> 00:27:56.542
if you're not killed
by Marseilles importers...


00:27:56.552 --> 00:27:59.163
or their people in the States...


00:27:59.514 --> 00:28:01.434
then, what?


00:28:01.917 --> 00:28:05.431
Then there'll be more, much more.
I guarantee you.


00:28:05.440 --> 00:28:10.116
And if it's all the same to you, I don't
have to drag my ass here no more.


00:28:10.125 --> 00:28:12.045
Of course not.


00:28:14.249 --> 00:28:16.165
My man.


00:28:16.175 --> 00:28:18.782
- Soul brothers?
- Soul brothers.


00:28:58.693 --> 00:29:03.809
Fifty grand. It'll cover them,
the pilot and the boys on the other end.


00:29:03.819 --> 00:29:05.739
Give them a hundred.


00:29:06.181 --> 00:29:08.101
Fifty will cover it.


00:29:08.144 --> 00:29:10.976
Give them a hundred, the whole thing.


00:29:10.986 --> 00:29:12.906
And look.


00:29:12.988 --> 00:29:14.300
That's all I got.


00:29:14.310 --> 00:29:17.818
If that dope don't arrive,
for any reason...


00:29:20.356 --> 00:29:21.747
Listen.


00:29:21.756 --> 00:29:24.430
Cousin or no cousin,
I'm a busy man, all right?


00:29:24.439 --> 00:29:27.622
I got no time to go
to nobody's funeral.


00:29:27.923 --> 00:29:30.556
I'll let you know
when it's in the air.


00:29:30.565 --> 00:29:32.485
My man.


00:29:54.509 --> 00:29:56.752
<i>Richie?
Fuckin' guy made me,</i>


00:29:57.032 --> 00:29:59.384
don't know how he did,
but he did.


00:29:59.394 --> 00:30:00.906
<i>He went for his gun!</i>


00:30:00.915 --> 00:30:02.387
I had to do it, man!


00:30:02.397 --> 00:30:03.989
A hundred people out there heard


00:30:03.999 --> 00:30:08.161
the shot. You gotta help me,
you gotta do something!


00:30:08.203 --> 00:30:10.123
Where are you, Jay?


00:30:10.565 --> 00:30:12.485
That's the problem.


00:30:15.090 --> 00:30:16.882
Dispatch, I got a 10-13.


00:30:16.892 --> 00:30:18.644
I got a 10-13.


00:30:18.653 --> 00:30:20.775
<i>Copy that. What's your 20?</i>


00:30:21.056 --> 00:30:22.976
Tower 2.


00:30:24.019 --> 00:30:25.939
Floor 1G.


00:30:26.181 --> 00:30:28.294
Canton West, in the projects.


00:30:28.303 --> 00:30:31.216
<i>- Identify yourself, please.
- Detective Richard Roberts.</i>


00:30:31.225 --> 00:30:33.698
<i>Negative, I got no units in that area.</i>


00:30:33.708 --> 00:30:35.340
Bullshit.


00:30:35.350 --> 00:30:37.863
Please put the call out again.
I'll need assistance.


00:30:37.872 --> 00:30:42.768
<i>Det. Roberts, I got no units
in that area, that's a negative.</i>


00:31:07.662 --> 00:31:10.355
Why you goin' thru, motherfucker?


00:31:11.026 --> 00:31:12.297
Be cool!


00:31:12.307 --> 00:31:13.899
Be cool, all right?


00:31:13.909 --> 00:31:17.010
I'll find out what's going on in here.


00:31:24.599 --> 00:31:26.519
Richie.


00:31:32.127 --> 00:31:33.959
<i>Open the motherfuckin' door!</i>


00:31:33.969 --> 00:31:35.889
Where's your backup?


00:31:36.691 --> 00:31:39.139
You got no backup?
Why is that?


00:31:42.337 --> 00:31:43.448
Bandage his neck.


00:31:43.457 --> 00:31:46.171
- Richie, he's dead.
- I know he's fuckin' dead, right?


00:31:46.181 --> 00:31:48.854
Bandage his neck, clean up his head.
Prop him up on the gurney


00:31:48.863 --> 00:31:51.256
so he's sittin,
and open his fuckin' eyes.


00:31:51.266 --> 00:31:53.632
- All right? Let's go!
- Fuck.


00:31:57.471 --> 00:31:59.391
OK, clean him up.


00:32:09.884 --> 00:32:11.156
Give me your gun.


00:32:11.166 --> 00:32:13.086
Your gun!


00:32:15.370 --> 00:32:17.290
You have your badge?


00:32:19.254 --> 00:32:20.645
You guys ready?


00:32:20.654 --> 00:32:22.694
Just keep moving forward.


00:32:23.258 --> 00:32:25.178
- You all right?
- Yeah.


00:32:26.460 --> 00:32:28.380
It's OK!


00:32:28.463 --> 00:32:31.156
Injured man coming out.
Step back.


00:32:33.307 --> 00:32:36.653
Let them do their job.
He'll be all right.


00:32:37.551 --> 00:32:39.471
Step back.


00:32:41.275 --> 00:32:43.195
That's fine.
That's it.


00:32:45.239 --> 00:32:47.159
He's alive.


00:32:47.602 --> 00:32:49.521
What happened inside?


00:32:59.334 --> 00:33:01.254
Thanks, man.


00:33:01.776 --> 00:33:03.608
Fuck.


00:33:03.618 --> 00:33:06.291
The asshole pulled a piece on me.
Can you fuckin' believe it?


00:33:06.300 --> 00:33:08.934
He pulls a piece on a cop?
Had to do it, man.


00:33:08.943 --> 00:33:10.863
Kill or be killed.


00:33:11.185 --> 00:33:13.388
Fuckin' crazy world, right?


00:33:15.870 --> 00:33:17.863
What the fuck were you doing
on the projects?


00:33:17.872 --> 00:33:20.646
Investigating stuff, man,
you know.


00:33:21.196 --> 00:33:22.948
Just like you taught me.


00:33:22.957 --> 00:33:25.590
Checking on guys,
following things up,


00:33:25.599 --> 00:33:27.872
putting the pieces together.


00:33:27.882 --> 00:33:31.717
The guy was a fucking dealer.
Scum of the earth!


00:33:32.326 --> 00:33:35.199
That guy
didn't pull a gun on a cop, Jay.


00:33:35.209 --> 00:33:37.762
That guy pulled a gun on a junkie.


00:33:37.772 --> 00:33:39.404
The junkie was trying to rob him.


00:33:39.413 --> 00:33:41.372
What the fuck you sayin?


00:33:42.296 --> 00:33:44.369
What the fuck you doin, man?


00:33:44.379 --> 00:33:46.731
- What the fuck is that?
- That money's mine, man!


00:33:46.740 --> 00:33:48.573
I earned this shit!
It's mine!


00:33:48.582 --> 00:33:50.454
I earned it doing good cop work.


00:33:50.464 --> 00:33:52.937
- I got it doin' good cop work!
- You murdered him!


00:33:52.947 --> 00:33:55.820
- And gettin' shot at!
- You murdered the guy!


00:33:55.829 --> 00:33:57.782
You murdered him,
you robbed his money,


00:33:57.792 --> 00:33:59.344
then you called me to get you out.


00:33:59.354 --> 00:34:01.065
Makes me an accessory after the fact.


00:34:01.075 --> 00:34:02.347
I'll tell you the facts,


00:34:02.356 --> 00:34:04.990
just write the report
the way i see it happened.


00:34:04.999 --> 00:34:06.871
And then that's the way it is.


00:34:06.881 --> 00:34:09.166
And that's how it'll all be.


00:34:09.843 --> 00:34:11.763
I can't do that.


00:34:12.206 --> 00:34:15.961
I'm a leper because I listened to you
and turned in a million bucks.


00:34:15.970 --> 00:34:18.563
No one will work with me after that.


00:34:18.573 --> 00:34:21.184
I can give up this shit, Richie!


00:34:21.375 --> 00:34:23.047
That's easy.


00:34:23.057 --> 00:34:24.977
Just write the report.


00:34:25.019 --> 00:34:26.410
Between us.


00:34:26.420 --> 00:34:28.340
As partners.


00:34:29.103 --> 00:34:31.023
I can't do that.


00:34:36.230 --> 00:34:38.150
Stop!


00:35:15.469 --> 00:35:17.389
Open the trunk.


00:35:38.572 --> 00:35:41.215
<i>Get out!
Get out of Vietnam!</i>


00:35:44.458 --> 00:35:47.611
<i>As loud as we can
that the Vietnam war should stop,</i>


00:35:47.621 --> 00:35:50.775
<i>and that the best way to stop it
is for the United States</i>


00:35:50.784 --> 00:35:54.864
<i>to simply pack up
and get out of Vietnam right now!</i>


00:35:59.272 --> 00:36:01.192
How are we looking?


00:36:03.477 --> 00:36:06.720
Typically what I see
is 25 to 45% pure.


00:36:07.041 --> 00:36:10.875
There are no adulterants, no alkaloids,
no dilutents.


00:36:10.885 --> 00:36:12.805
It's a hundred percent.


00:36:17.411 --> 00:36:19.614
- May I?
- Take it with you.


00:36:20.894 --> 00:36:22.814
Thank you, Frank.


00:38:14.007 --> 00:38:15.198
I'll take it.


00:38:15.208 --> 00:38:18.227
No contingencies, no loan,
no nothing.


00:38:18.932 --> 00:38:20.852
Cash.


00:38:21.094 --> 00:38:23.014
Fabulous.


00:38:26.979 --> 00:38:29.292
I'm not talking
about your proclivities.


00:38:29.302 --> 00:38:33.257
Those I only know too well.
I'm talking about being a cop.


00:38:33.266 --> 00:38:35.659
You talking about taking money?


00:38:35.668 --> 00:38:37.260
I don't do that.
Not my thing.


00:38:37.270 --> 00:38:40.223
And your friends from the hood,
still hang out with them?


00:38:40.233 --> 00:38:42.186
Yeah. Play baseball on the weekends.


00:38:42.195 --> 00:38:44.725
Wise guys?
It's gonna look good.


00:38:44.957 --> 00:38:47.271
Guys I went to school with, so what?


00:38:47.280 --> 00:38:49.320
What about Joseph Sadano?


00:38:50.483 --> 00:38:51.715
What about him?


00:38:51.724 --> 00:38:54.357
I'm just trying to understand
things your wife has said.


00:38:54.367 --> 00:38:57.401
- If they're not true, tell me.
- Yeah, he's one of them.


00:38:57.410 --> 00:38:59.923
Is he also your son's godfather?


00:38:59.932 --> 00:39:01.685
He's definitely fucking her.


00:39:01.695 --> 00:39:03.887
Do you really care about this?


00:39:03.897 --> 00:39:07.079
Or do you just not want her
to win ever?


00:39:09.783 --> 00:39:13.096
You know there's an interview room?
On the second floor.


00:39:13.105 --> 00:39:15.498
- That's what I thought.
- Door locks from the inside.


00:39:15.508 --> 00:39:17.428
All rise!


00:39:24.437 --> 00:39:27.130
Fuck me like a cop, not a lawyer.


00:39:35.808 --> 00:39:37.728
Don't answer!


00:39:57.590 --> 00:39:59.956
- Richie Roberts.
- Hey, Norm!


00:40:02.154 --> 00:40:04.307
- Richie Roberts.
- Hi, Det. Norman Riley.


00:40:04.316 --> 00:40:07.009
- Hi, Norman. How are you?
- Good.


00:40:07.199 --> 00:40:09.119
- Is that him?
- Yeah.


00:40:16.649 --> 00:40:20.163
Nice night to come out, huh?
It's like Grand Central around here.


00:40:20.172 --> 00:40:21.845
It's been like this.


00:40:21.854 --> 00:40:24.127
I'm lucky if I get home by midnight.


00:40:24.136 --> 00:40:27.074
It's like nothing we've seen before.


00:40:30.823 --> 00:40:32.495
Something I gotta sign?


00:40:32.505 --> 00:40:34.425
Yeah, this way.


00:40:34.666 --> 00:40:38.910
I'm taking this with me.
I'll register it, all right?


00:40:40.713 --> 00:40:43.226
<i>America's public enemy number one</i>


00:40:43.235 --> 00:40:46.010
<i>in the United States
is drug abuse.</i>


00:40:47.360 --> 00:40:49.352
<i>In order
to fight and defeat this enemy,</i>


00:40:49.361 --> 00:40:51.281
<i>It is necessary to wage</i>


00:40:51.604 --> 00:40:53.562
<i>a new all out offensive.</i>


00:40:54.527 --> 00:40:57.039
<i>Federal authorities
have announced their intention</i>


00:40:57.049 --> 00:41:00.363
<i>to establish special
narcotics bureaus in Washington</i>


00:41:00.372 --> 00:41:02.325
<i>New York, Los Angeles, Chicago...</i>


00:41:02.335 --> 00:41:04.207
A detective without the support


00:41:04.216 --> 00:41:07.888
of his fellow detectives
really can't do much.


00:41:08.340 --> 00:41:10.707
You know why I don't have it.


00:41:11.103 --> 00:41:14.056
Doesn't matter.
You do what you have to do.


00:41:14.066 --> 00:41:18.021
The greatest city in the world
is turning into an open sewer.


00:41:18.030 --> 00:41:19.950
Everybody's stealing.


00:41:20.353 --> 00:41:22.273
Dealing.


00:41:22.555 --> 00:41:25.737
You can't work
because you did your job!


00:41:25.918 --> 00:41:29.191
Good news is you're not
the only honest cop in town.


00:41:29.201 --> 00:41:31.233
This special narcotics bureau
in Washington


00:41:31.243 --> 00:41:33.446
is not a dog and pony show.


00:41:33.806 --> 00:41:35.077
They're sincere.


00:41:35.087 --> 00:41:37.159
I know it because
they want us to orchestrate it


00:41:37.169 --> 00:41:39.642
and I want you
to head up things here on our end.


00:41:39.652 --> 00:41:41.283
If it's federal,
who do I answer to?


00:41:41.293 --> 00:41:43.006
- Post office?
- You answer to me.


00:41:43.015 --> 00:41:46.035
Me and the U.S. Attorney,
nobody else.


00:41:47.259 --> 00:41:49.692
You never step foot
in a police station again,


00:41:49.702 --> 00:41:51.173
work out at your own place.


00:41:51.183 --> 00:41:52.535
You pick your own guys,


00:41:52.544 --> 00:41:57.277
Guys that you know wouldn't
take a nickel off the sidewalk.


00:42:17.289 --> 00:42:19.122
<i>- Huey.
- Huey!</i>


00:42:19.131 --> 00:42:20.803
<i>- What of what?
- Who's this?</i>


00:42:20.812 --> 00:42:22.525
Who you think, boy?


00:42:22.535 --> 00:42:24.455
<i>- Frank!
- Frank who?</i>


00:42:24.496 --> 00:42:26.416
<i>Your brother, negro.</i>


00:42:29.861 --> 00:42:31.820
- That's right.
- Marvin!


00:42:31.943 --> 00:42:33.455
- Where's Ma?
- What?


00:42:33.465 --> 00:42:35.538
Where's...
Frank's on the phone!


00:42:35.547 --> 00:42:36.939
How you doin, Frankie?


00:42:36.949 --> 00:42:38.869
Frank, on the phone!


00:42:39.311 --> 00:42:41.864
- Say what?
- Ma, Frank on the phone!


00:42:41.874 --> 00:42:43.065
Oh, my Lord!


00:42:43.075 --> 00:42:45.227
Yo, when?
You just say it, man.


00:42:45.237 --> 00:42:46.549
<i>I'll call you back</i>


00:42:46.558 --> 00:42:49.031
at 6 o'clock.
Get everybody together, all right?


00:42:49.041 --> 00:42:50.961
Mama, everybody.


00:43:10.623 --> 00:43:12.744
How you doin, Uncle Frank?


00:43:12.824 --> 00:43:15.190
Get out of the car!
It's here.


00:43:16.027 --> 00:43:17.899
Look at this!


00:43:17.909 --> 00:43:19.461
My Lord!


00:43:19.471 --> 00:43:21.429
So glad to see you, boy.


00:43:21.994 --> 00:43:26.037
I'm telling you,
some piece of land you got here.


00:43:27.439 --> 00:43:30.072
- I wonder what the Boro people'd say.
- And whose house is that?


00:43:30.082 --> 00:43:32.122
That is your house, Mama.


00:43:32.564 --> 00:43:34.484
- Mine?
- That's yours.


00:43:35.608 --> 00:43:37.528
And who else?


00:43:51.223 --> 00:43:52.334
Listen!


00:43:52.344 --> 00:43:54.576
I wanna tell you how happy I am.


00:43:54.586 --> 00:43:56.658
Seeing all my children at the table,


00:43:56.668 --> 00:43:59.141
and the grand children
at the same time.


00:43:59.150 --> 00:44:00.622
I'm so happy!


00:44:00.632 --> 00:44:02.944
- Right on, Grandma!
- Enjoy yourselves.


00:44:02.954 --> 00:44:05.307
I hope you got a job,
the way you eatin' all this.


00:44:05.317 --> 00:44:07.846
That boy, he got an arm on him.


00:44:08.000 --> 00:44:09.231
A Major League arm.


00:44:09.241 --> 00:44:11.161
- Oh yeah?
- Right?


00:44:11.523 --> 00:44:12.795
Right on, Pop.


00:44:12.804 --> 00:44:15.637
After dinner,
let's see him throw around a bit.


00:44:15.647 --> 00:44:17.119
You can't catch him, man.


00:44:17.128 --> 00:44:20.402
I'm telling you,
he throws harder than Gibson.


00:44:20.411 --> 00:44:22.604
We're talking 95 miles an hour.


00:44:22.614 --> 00:44:24.534
Can you catch him?


00:44:24.856 --> 00:44:26.408
He'd go catch the grass.


00:44:26.417 --> 00:44:29.251
He might have catched that thing
when I was about 5 years old.


00:44:29.261 --> 00:44:31.627
Since then, he can't keep up.


00:44:34.306 --> 00:44:35.978
This is your room.


00:44:35.987 --> 00:44:37.907
Perfect.


00:44:39.831 --> 00:44:41.751
Look at this.


00:44:43.955 --> 00:44:45.387
It's beautiful.


00:44:45.396 --> 00:44:47.316
Real beautiful, this.


00:44:54.967 --> 00:44:56.398
How did you...


00:44:56.408 --> 00:44:58.327
I had it made.


00:44:59.451 --> 00:45:00.762
From memory.


00:45:00.772 --> 00:45:02.484
You were 5 when they took it away.


00:45:02.494 --> 00:45:03.966
- Right.
- How could you...


00:45:03.975 --> 00:45:06.097
How could I forget, Mamma?


00:45:10.141 --> 00:45:12.061
I thought you did.


00:45:12.463 --> 00:45:14.335
It, it... is perfect.


00:45:14.345 --> 00:45:16.265
It's all perfect.


00:45:21.272 --> 00:45:23.945
I can't tell you
how much I love you.


00:45:23.955 --> 00:45:25.875
I love you too, Mother.


00:45:26.638 --> 00:45:28.558
It's okay.


00:45:35.766 --> 00:45:39.521
Both these guys, good with wires.
They got solid informants.


00:45:39.531 --> 00:45:40.962
They're honest.


00:45:40.971 --> 00:45:42.444
And fearless.


00:45:42.454 --> 00:45:45.065
They're insane, Richie,
like you.


00:45:45.256 --> 00:45:47.176
Where are they?


00:45:49.620 --> 00:45:52.253
That's Jones,
with the skinny white broad.


00:45:52.263 --> 00:45:54.096
Best I've ever seen on the street.


00:45:54.105 --> 00:45:56.716
He knows dope,
but he's together.


00:45:57.829 --> 00:46:00.061
He's a stand up guy, all around.


00:46:00.071 --> 00:46:01.543
That's Abruzzo


00:46:01.553 --> 00:46:03.745
with the two black fat ones.


00:46:03.755 --> 00:46:05.957
He loves a big ass, man.


00:46:07.719 --> 00:46:09.511
He's a bulldog.


00:46:09.521 --> 00:46:12.313
He don't fuck around,
he got a bit of a temper yeah, but,


00:46:12.323 --> 00:46:14.956
you could trust this guy
with your grandma.


00:46:14.966 --> 00:46:16.238
Listen.


00:46:16.247 --> 00:46:20.817
We work together. You want me,
you got to take them, too.


00:46:31.222 --> 00:46:33.142
When do we start?


00:46:35.306 --> 00:46:36.658
<i>The man I worked for</i>


00:46:36.668 --> 00:46:40.942
ran one of the biggest companies
in New York City for more than 50 years.


00:46:40.952 --> 00:46:42.503
15 years,


00:46:42.513 --> 00:46:44.433
8 months and 9 days


00:46:44.676 --> 00:46:46.227
I was with him every day,


00:46:46.237 --> 00:46:50.398
protected him, looked after him.
I learned from him.


00:46:50.481 --> 00:46:52.874
Bumpy was rich,
but wasn't white man rich.


00:46:52.884 --> 00:46:54.636
He wasn't wealthy.


00:46:54.645 --> 00:46:56.798
He didn't own his own company.
He thought he did.


00:46:56.807 --> 00:46:58.439
He just managed it.


00:46:58.449 --> 00:47:00.882
White men owned it,
so they owned him.


00:47:00.891 --> 00:47:02.403
Nobody owns me though.


00:47:02.413 --> 00:47:04.286
- How you doin, babe?
- Good.


00:47:04.295 --> 00:47:07.128
Cause I own my own company,
and my company sells a product


00:47:07.138 --> 00:47:10.011
that's better than the competition's.


00:47:10.021 --> 00:47:13.735
At a price that's lower
than the competition's.


00:47:13.745 --> 00:47:15.785
What are we selling here?


00:47:30.321 --> 00:47:32.241
How you doin, Red?


00:47:32.283 --> 00:47:34.275
My brothers,
just got here from North Carolina,


00:47:34.285 --> 00:47:36.205
Guys, this is Redtop.


00:47:36.367 --> 00:47:37.959
- How you doin?
- And the ladies.


00:47:37.968 --> 00:47:39.280
Nice family.


00:47:39.290 --> 00:47:42.283
What? Ya'll niggas
never seen hoochie before?


00:47:42.293 --> 00:47:43.604
Why they all naked?


00:47:43.614 --> 00:47:45.735
So they can steal nothin'.


00:47:47.778 --> 00:47:50.652
Most important thing in business
is honesty.


00:47:50.661 --> 00:47:52.581
Integrity, hard work.


00:47:53.424 --> 00:47:55.344
Family.


00:47:55.466 --> 00:47:57.659
Never forgetting
where we came from.


00:47:57.668 --> 00:47:59.588
Thank you, Charlene.


00:48:04.035 --> 00:48:07.148
See, you are what you are
in this world.


00:48:07.158 --> 00:48:09.769
That's either one of two things.


00:48:10.521 --> 00:48:12.441
Either you're somebody.


00:48:13.364 --> 00:48:15.731
Or nobody.
I'll be right back.


00:48:30.901 --> 00:48:32.172
I need this fresh,


00:48:32.182 --> 00:48:34.375
cause if I come back here,
you'll know what it is.


00:48:34.384 --> 00:48:36.057
- You don't play that.
- I hear you,


00:48:36.066 --> 00:48:39.540
you won't have to come back.
There will be no problem.


00:48:39.550 --> 00:48:40.741
Where's my money?


00:48:40.751 --> 00:48:43.344
Redtop gave you the package,
you supposed to hand me my money.


00:48:43.353 --> 00:48:45.266
Here's a jar right here.
20%.


00:48:45.275 --> 00:48:47.968
- You got the jar?
- That's right.


00:48:48.359 --> 00:48:49.831
Get the fuck outta here...


00:48:49.840 --> 00:48:53.114
What you gonna do?
What the fuck you gonna do?


00:48:53.123 --> 00:48:54.315
What you doin?


00:48:54.324 --> 00:48:56.397
You wanna shoot me,
in front of everybody?


00:48:56.407 --> 00:48:58.327
Huh? Come on!


00:49:00.090 --> 00:49:02.010
Shit.


00:49:12.783 --> 00:49:14.415
Here you go.


00:49:14.425 --> 00:49:16.345
20%.


00:49:38.209 --> 00:49:40.129
So, what was I sayin?


00:49:49.940 --> 00:49:54.265
This is the newly formed
Essex County narcotics squad.


00:49:54.464 --> 00:49:58.707
Our mandate is to make major arrests.
No street guys.


00:49:59.029 --> 00:50:02.022
We're looking for the suppliers
and the distributors.


00:50:02.032 --> 00:50:03.784
Heroin, cocaine, amphetamines.


00:50:03.793 --> 00:50:06.787
No grass under 1,000 pounds.
No powder under 40 kilos.


00:50:06.796 --> 00:50:08.909
Less than that,
someone else can waste their time.


00:50:08.919 --> 00:50:11.152
We'll be handling big shipments,
big money,


00:50:11.161 --> 00:50:12.473
and big temptation.


00:50:12.482 --> 00:50:14.635
I heard a story about you.
That you found


00:50:14.644 --> 00:50:17.999
a million dollars in unmarked cash.
And you gave that shit back.


00:50:18.008 --> 00:50:19.800
Is that true?


00:50:19.810 --> 00:50:23.319
Yeah, I did.
Anyone got a problem with that?


00:50:26.777 --> 00:50:28.849
So do I.
I think about it everyday.


00:50:28.859 --> 00:50:31.852
I should be down in Florida with
a 68 full cruiser dual, fishing sharks.


00:50:31.862 --> 00:50:33.573
- You and me both.
- But you know...


00:50:33.583 --> 00:50:36.031
I didn't, so here I am, and...


00:50:36.947 --> 00:50:40.293
We'll try to land
some other kinda sharks.


00:51:04.935 --> 00:51:06.855
- All right?
- Bingo.


00:51:29.199 --> 00:51:31.119
See that?


00:51:31.481 --> 00:51:34.114
And this stuff is everyday's stuff.


00:51:34.123 --> 00:51:35.635
But this Blue Magic,


00:51:35.645 --> 00:51:37.238
twice the potency.


00:51:37.247 --> 00:51:39.759
The purest thing
I've ever seen in the street.


00:51:39.769 --> 00:51:41.689
Strong enough to smoke.


00:51:41.851 --> 00:51:44.765
That's for those suburban
white kids scared of needles.


00:51:44.774 --> 00:51:46.526
You paid 10 bucks for that?


00:51:46.536 --> 00:51:49.049
And it's everywhere,
on every corner.


00:51:49.059 --> 00:51:50.979
So how's that possible?


00:51:51.061 --> 00:51:55.793
Who can afford to sell shit
twice as good for half as much?


00:52:02.151 --> 00:52:04.594
Hey man, good to see you!


00:52:04.914 --> 00:52:06.747
- Doin' good?
- Yeah, just got back


00:52:06.756 --> 00:52:09.612
from a trip to the south of France.


00:52:22.812 --> 00:52:24.732
Know what I'm sayin?


00:52:25.575 --> 00:52:27.495
Here you go!


00:52:31.341 --> 00:52:33.261
Who is that?


00:52:43.513 --> 00:52:45.345
Ladies and gentlemen.


00:52:45.355 --> 00:52:47.640
The Proud Bomber, the champ.


00:52:48.037 --> 00:52:49.957
Mr. Joe Louis!


00:52:58.368 --> 00:53:00.079
Who's that with Joe?


00:53:00.089 --> 00:53:02.009
Miss Puerto Rico.


00:53:02.092 --> 00:53:03.844
Puerto Rico?


00:53:03.853 --> 00:53:07.607
- She a beauty queen.
- Real. The beauty queen.


00:53:31.841 --> 00:53:33.761
My main man.


00:53:38.167 --> 00:53:39.960
Excuse us for a minute, please.


00:53:39.969 --> 00:53:41.889
Sure, Frank.


00:53:43.492 --> 00:53:45.412
Thank you.


00:53:48.657 --> 00:53:49.849
What's goin' on?


00:53:49.859 --> 00:53:51.170
What you smiling about?


00:53:51.180 --> 00:53:52.852
- I dunno.
- What is this?


00:53:52.862 --> 00:53:54.293
What's what?


00:53:54.303 --> 00:53:56.223
- What?
- Come here.


00:53:57.787 --> 00:53:59.179
What's that you wearin'?


00:53:59.188 --> 00:54:01.060
What's what?


00:54:01.070 --> 00:54:02.742
That, what you got on?


00:54:02.752 --> 00:54:04.464
A very, very, very nice suit.


00:54:04.473 --> 00:54:05.985
Very, very nice suit, huh?


00:54:05.995 --> 00:54:07.868
That's a clown suit,
a costume, man,


00:54:07.877 --> 00:54:10.150
with a big sign that says:
"Arrest me".


00:54:10.159 --> 00:54:12.712
Understand? You too loud,
you're making too much noise.


00:54:12.721 --> 00:54:15.154
Look at me.
The loudest one in the room


00:54:15.164 --> 00:54:18.478
is the weakest one in the room,
I tell you that.


00:54:18.487 --> 00:54:21.441
- You tryin' to be like Nicky Barnes?
- What's the problem with him?


00:54:21.451 --> 00:54:23.843
- I like him.
- I got no problem. You like him?


00:54:23.853 --> 00:54:26.005
You wanna be like him?
You wanna be Superfly?


00:54:26.014 --> 00:54:27.526
You wanna work for him?


00:54:27.536 --> 00:54:29.328
Share a jail cell with him?
Cook for him?


00:54:29.338 --> 00:54:32.532
- He wants to talk to you.
- So, you talkin' to him about me now?


00:54:32.541 --> 00:54:33.933
What about?


00:54:33.943 --> 00:54:35.655
- It ain't like that.
- Then what is it?


00:54:35.664 --> 00:54:38.097
- Your name came up.
- About what?


00:54:38.107 --> 00:54:41.207
I don't know, I told him I'd tell you.


00:54:42.592 --> 00:54:44.512
You know, boy...


00:54:45.955 --> 00:54:48.387
If you wasn't my bro', I'd kill you.
You know that?


00:54:48.397 --> 00:54:50.469
I'd blow your fuckin' brains out.


00:54:50.479 --> 00:54:52.832
- Don't be like that.
- I'm taking you shoppin' this week.


00:54:52.842 --> 00:54:55.534
- I can do it alone.
- I can tell.


00:55:27.036 --> 00:55:28.668
You still owe me that dance.


00:55:28.677 --> 00:55:30.029
Doc, come on.


00:55:30.039 --> 00:55:31.591
Frank.


00:55:31.600 --> 00:55:33.520
Check this.


00:55:42.691 --> 00:55:44.364
- How you doing?
- Hi.


00:55:44.373 --> 00:55:46.495
- Frank Lucas.
- Eva Jendo.


00:55:47.055 --> 00:55:48.407
Nice to meet you, Eva.


00:55:48.417 --> 00:55:50.375
Nice to meet you, Frank.


00:55:51.100 --> 00:55:53.173
You're Frank,
and this is your place.


00:55:53.182 --> 00:55:56.773
That's right, I'm Frank
and this is my place.


00:56:01.429 --> 00:56:03.342
Why is it called Small's?


00:56:03.351 --> 00:56:05.271
Why not Frank's?


00:56:06.435 --> 00:56:09.909
When you own something,
you call it what you want.


00:56:09.919 --> 00:56:11.390
Small's.


00:56:11.400 --> 00:56:13.032
Or Frank's.


00:56:13.042 --> 00:56:14.434
Frankie Small's.


00:56:14.443 --> 00:56:16.363
Small's Frankie.


00:56:17.286 --> 00:56:19.206
That's right.


00:56:19.287 --> 00:56:21.490
You want to let my hand go?


00:56:22.771 --> 00:56:24.691
Okay.


00:56:25.053 --> 00:56:26.365
You're leaving?


00:56:26.375 --> 00:56:28.087
No, I was going to my table.


00:56:28.096 --> 00:56:30.707
You need someone to go with you?


00:56:32.301 --> 00:56:34.221
Yes?


00:56:39.508 --> 00:56:41.340
Wash your hand?
I got one print of that.


00:56:41.350 --> 00:56:43.270
You'll smudge it.


00:56:44.393 --> 00:56:46.505
- Here you go.
- What about him?


00:56:46.515 --> 00:56:48.067
- Who's that?
- Joey Sadano.


00:56:48.077 --> 00:56:49.788
Don Cattano's nephew.


00:56:49.798 --> 00:56:52.471
- Put him up there by the big man
- He looks like you, Abruzzo.


00:56:52.481 --> 00:56:53.632
Not as handsome.


00:56:53.642 --> 00:56:55.995
- Looks more like your sister.
- Where's Ice Pick Paul?


00:56:56.004 --> 00:56:58.357
Funny. You guys should
take that show on the road.


00:56:58.367 --> 00:57:00.570
So we need...
Ice Pick Paul.


00:57:01.890 --> 00:57:03.810
There you go.


00:57:04.293 --> 00:57:06.165
He goes near the top.


00:57:06.174 --> 00:57:09.288
No, Ice Pick Paul is a soldier,
this guy is a lieutenant.


00:57:09.297 --> 00:57:13.212
"...you have passed the
New Jersey Bar Examination."


00:57:13.222 --> 00:57:14.773
That guy is a soldier.


00:57:14.783 --> 00:57:16.815
This guy's a lieutenant.
No way he's on top.


00:57:16.825 --> 00:57:19.178
You're thinking Benny the Bishop.
Benny Two Socks,


00:57:19.187 --> 00:57:22.341
- Cattano's deadbeat son-in-law.
- Jonesy's right.


00:57:22.350 --> 00:57:25.904
Which one of you has actually seen
Ice Pick Paul selling drugs?


00:57:25.914 --> 00:57:27.105
Actually,


00:57:27.115 --> 00:57:29.067
- seen it go down?
- Yeah, seen it go down,


00:57:29.077 --> 00:57:31.270
been in his place,
seen him handle drugs?


00:57:31.279 --> 00:57:33.192
That rat Rickie has told us.


00:57:33.201 --> 00:57:34.793
He's fuckin' dead!


00:57:34.803 --> 00:57:36.722
About 4 weeks ago.


00:57:37.646 --> 00:57:38.837
He's dead.


00:57:38.847 --> 00:57:40.999
Well, we can take him
off the fuckin' board.


00:57:41.009 --> 00:57:43.882
I don't think
we got any solid evidence


00:57:43.892 --> 00:57:45.804
on anybody on that board.


00:57:45.814 --> 00:57:48.727
What you saying?
This is weeks and weeks of work, man.


00:57:48.737 --> 00:57:52.817
I say take it down.
We start again from the street.


00:57:54.182 --> 00:57:58.017
That's considerably more
than one year's salary.


00:57:58.546 --> 00:58:00.419
If it disappears...


00:58:00.429 --> 00:58:03.774
we'll not be able
to get it for you again.


00:58:03.832 --> 00:58:05.143
That's yours.


00:58:05.153 --> 00:58:07.426
Sign on my life for you again?


00:58:07.436 --> 00:58:09.476
For a lousy twenty grand?


00:58:12.200 --> 00:58:14.192
It has to be Blue Magic, OK?


00:58:14.202 --> 00:58:15.914
It's gonna be Blue.


00:58:15.924 --> 00:58:18.237
- Pick it up here tomorrow.
- $20,000.


00:58:18.246 --> 00:58:20.166
Just leave it there.


00:58:33.381 --> 00:58:35.301
- How did it go?
- Good.


00:58:37.185 --> 00:58:38.657
Here he comes.


00:58:38.666 --> 00:58:40.586
- That's him?
- Yeah.


00:58:41.189 --> 00:58:43.109
He's quick.


00:58:53.722 --> 00:58:56.634
- He goes into the City. What do we do?
- Stay with the fuckin' money.


00:58:56.644 --> 00:58:58.357
We stay with the money, all right?


00:58:58.366 --> 00:59:00.238
- We can't go there!
- Yes, we can.


00:59:00.248 --> 00:59:02.400
That's 20 grand in there
that I'm responsible for.


00:59:02.410 --> 00:59:05.443
- I ain't losin' it, follow the money!
- It's out of our jurisdiction!


00:59:05.453 --> 00:59:07.983
- Follow the money!
- All right!


00:59:21.669 --> 00:59:23.181
He's pulling over.


00:59:23.191 --> 00:59:25.111
All right, here we go.


00:59:25.233 --> 00:59:27.153
Let me out here.


00:59:28.756 --> 00:59:33.081
- Don't disappear, all right?
- I'll circle the block.


01:00:08.556 --> 01:00:10.476
Sit down!


01:00:11.599 --> 01:00:14.112
Happy birthday, gentlemen.
How you doin?


01:00:14.122 --> 01:00:17.957
<i>You're up to something, huh?
He's going bowling.</i>


01:00:18.406 --> 01:00:20.158
Look at that.
Right between the legs.


01:00:20.168 --> 01:00:21.759
- What's in the bag?
- Nothing.


01:00:21.769 --> 01:00:23.041
Get the fuck up!


01:00:23.050 --> 01:00:25.643
<i>- It's my bag.
- Shut the fuck up! What did I tell you?</i>


01:00:25.653 --> 01:00:27.645
<i>- Keep your your head down!
- What you doin?</i>


01:00:27.655 --> 01:00:30.919
<i>- Sit down and shut up!
- Don't you move!</i>


01:00:42.069 --> 01:00:43.301
Hey guys!


01:00:43.310 --> 01:00:45.230
Guys! Officers!


01:00:45.793 --> 01:00:47.914
I'm Richie Roberts.
Newark.


01:00:49.677 --> 01:00:51.597
That's... my money.


01:00:51.999 --> 01:00:54.039
What the fuck?
What money?


01:00:55.963 --> 01:00:58.556
The bills are sequenced,
they're registered with the Essex


01:00:58.566 --> 01:01:00.118
County Prosecutors Office.


01:01:00.127 --> 01:01:02.960
Check them up.
They all start with CF3500.


01:01:02.970 --> 01:01:04.890
Have a look.


01:01:08.816 --> 01:01:10.168
Fucking registers.


01:01:10.178 --> 01:01:13.171
I thought I had a fucking Chris-Craft
sitting in my driveway.


01:01:13.180 --> 01:01:14.652
Honest mistake.


01:01:14.662 --> 01:01:16.620
I'll just get the money.


01:01:17.665 --> 01:01:19.585
This time.


01:01:22.589 --> 01:01:26.669
When's the last time I was in Jersey?
Let me think.


01:01:27.274 --> 01:01:29.194
Never.


01:01:30.277 --> 01:01:32.510
What're you doing coming over here
unannounced?


01:01:32.520 --> 01:01:35.457
You know you can get hurt
doing that?


01:01:36.323 --> 01:01:38.276
You got your fucking money.


01:01:38.285 --> 01:01:40.037
Richie.


01:01:40.047 --> 01:01:41.559
And never ever


01:01:41.569 --> 01:01:43.801
come into this city again unannounced.


01:01:43.811 --> 01:01:46.203
You come in to see
a fuckin' Broadway show?


01:01:46.213 --> 01:01:50.130
You call ahead first to see
if it's okay with me.


01:01:50.418 --> 01:01:52.338
No problem.


01:01:56.223 --> 01:01:58.916
- Go hit some ball.
- Great suits.


01:02:00.948 --> 01:02:02.868
Is that your car?


01:02:03.030 --> 01:02:04.862
Fucking great car.


01:02:04.871 --> 01:02:07.505
Have a nice fuckin' trip
back to Jersey.


01:02:07.514 --> 01:02:08.786
All right.


01:02:08.796 --> 01:02:11.652
Come on, I got a tea time.
Let's go.


01:02:23.251 --> 01:02:25.171
This is your father?


01:02:25.853 --> 01:02:27.975
That's Martin Luther King.


01:02:28.456 --> 01:02:30.368
- It is not.
- Yes, it is Martin Luther King.


01:02:30.378 --> 01:02:33.211
- You know, "I have a dream".
- Of course.


01:02:33.220 --> 01:02:35.052
No, that's...


01:02:35.061 --> 01:02:37.655
He was just as important
as Martin Luther King.


01:02:37.665 --> 01:02:39.705
- To me.
- What did he do?


01:02:40.507 --> 01:02:43.363
A lot of things, he was a...
friend.


01:02:43.990 --> 01:02:46.928
Served New York,
New York served him.


01:02:47.314 --> 01:02:49.187
He was my boss.


01:02:49.196 --> 01:02:50.587
My teacher.


01:02:50.597 --> 01:02:52.190
What did he teach you?


01:02:52.199 --> 01:02:55.055
He taught me a lot of things. He...


01:02:56.323 --> 01:02:58.771
Taught me how to take my time.


01:02:59.686 --> 01:03:04.321
That if I was going to do something,
to do it with care, love.


01:03:04.331 --> 01:03:06.251
Anything else?


01:03:10.177 --> 01:03:12.289
Taught me to be a gentleman.


01:03:12.299 --> 01:03:13.571
That's what you are?


01:03:13.580 --> 01:03:16.355
That's what I try to be.
Come here.


01:03:17.024 --> 01:03:18.944
Come sit here.


01:03:21.067 --> 01:03:22.987
Look at me.


01:03:23.190 --> 01:03:26.454
I own about five apartments
in Manhattan.


01:03:27.434 --> 01:03:30.067
Homes all over the East Coast.
Could've taken you to anyone of 'em,


01:03:30.077 --> 01:03:32.688
but I didn't.
I brought you here.


01:03:32.759 --> 01:03:36.153
- I was looking for you, boy.
- Cause I want you to meet my mother.


01:03:36.162 --> 01:03:37.795
How you doin, Ma?


01:03:37.805 --> 01:03:39.637
- Is this her?
- Eva,


01:03:39.646 --> 01:03:41.599
- this is my mother.
- Hi, Eva.


01:03:41.608 --> 01:03:43.040
Nice to meet you.


01:03:43.049 --> 01:03:44.922
She's beautiful.


01:03:44.932 --> 01:03:46.243
Look at her.


01:03:46.253 --> 01:03:47.765
She's an angel


01:03:47.774 --> 01:03:49.694
come down from Heaven.


01:03:49.737 --> 01:03:51.657
Thank you.


01:03:58.585 --> 01:04:00.097
Mr. Roberts.


01:04:00.107 --> 01:04:02.473
I'm here for our appointment.


01:04:06.033 --> 01:04:07.953
- Morning.
- Morning.


01:04:09.636 --> 01:04:11.556
Sorry, our appointment?


01:04:11.839 --> 01:04:13.759
Child Social Services.


01:04:27.414 --> 01:04:30.106
She did mention your name though.


01:04:30.337 --> 01:04:32.866
- The stewardess?
- No, not her.


01:04:34.020 --> 01:04:37.534
The lady from Social Services,
she mentioned your name.


01:04:37.544 --> 01:04:39.336
Right after she asked me


01:04:39.345 --> 01:04:41.538
if I associated with any criminals.


01:04:41.548 --> 01:04:43.701
- All right, go!
- You want to see this?


01:04:43.711 --> 01:04:45.422
Hey, boys!


01:04:45.432 --> 01:04:47.264
Joey!


01:04:47.274 --> 01:04:49.194
Get in the pool.


01:04:49.956 --> 01:04:51.876
Come on!


01:04:56.043 --> 01:04:57.754
How'd she get my name?


01:04:57.764 --> 01:04:59.684
Laurie.


01:05:00.206 --> 01:05:02.736
She's been saying a lot lately.


01:05:03.249 --> 01:05:05.169
A lot.


01:05:08.135 --> 01:05:10.527
When you asked me to be
your son's godfather,


01:05:10.537 --> 01:05:12.409
- I took it very seriously.
- I know.


01:05:12.418 --> 01:05:13.891
And I appreciate that.


01:05:13.900 --> 01:05:16.733
And I said yes, I would take on
that responsibility


01:05:16.743 --> 01:05:19.416
to take care of your son, if God forbid,
something happened to you.


01:05:19.425 --> 01:05:22.018
Jo, the things she said
to Child Social Services


01:05:22.028 --> 01:05:23.700
make me look really bad.


01:05:23.710 --> 01:05:24.901
You know.


01:05:24.911 --> 01:05:26.904
All kinds at the house at night time,


01:05:26.913 --> 01:05:29.426
low life informants around.
Women...


01:05:29.435 --> 01:05:31.355
Old friends like me.


01:05:31.798 --> 01:05:34.001
Old friends like you, yeah.


01:05:35.562 --> 01:05:37.482
Uncle Joey!
Watch me!


01:05:41.208 --> 01:05:42.519
I understand.


01:05:42.529 --> 01:05:45.162
They ask me, I'll tell them
what you want me to tell.


01:05:45.171 --> 01:05:47.324
- I'll lie for you.
- Don't lie.


01:05:47.333 --> 01:05:48.685
You don't have to lie.


01:05:48.695 --> 01:05:51.417
Just... omit certain details.


01:05:52.258 --> 01:05:54.178
Sure, all right.


01:05:56.262 --> 01:05:58.415
I have something else to ask you.


01:05:58.424 --> 01:06:01.851
You don't have to answer
if you don't want.


01:06:03.509 --> 01:06:04.822
Blue Magic.


01:06:04.831 --> 01:06:06.751
Anything?


01:06:07.353 --> 01:06:12.983
A lot of sorrow, misery from guys
getting put out of work. That's all.


01:06:13.039 --> 01:06:14.791
What, your guys?


01:06:14.801 --> 01:06:16.721
His guys.


01:06:17.123 --> 01:06:19.734
You know where it's comin' from?


01:06:19.965 --> 01:06:22.821
Guys down south,
that's all I heard.


01:06:23.009 --> 01:06:24.929
- Cubans?
- I dunno.


01:06:25.812 --> 01:06:27.524
Or Mexico?


01:06:27.533 --> 01:06:29.126
Don't know.


01:06:29.135 --> 01:06:31.408
You're telling me
it's from South America?


01:06:31.417 --> 01:06:33.337
I don't know!


01:06:33.620 --> 01:06:38.455
Whoever it is, they're upsetting
the natural order of things.


01:06:38.465 --> 01:06:40.385
That's all there is.


01:06:55.121 --> 01:06:56.793
<i>- What's up?
- My man.</i>


01:06:56.802 --> 01:06:58.722
<i>How's it lookin?</i>


01:08:23.729 --> 01:08:25.562
I want you to meet Mike Sobota.


01:08:25.571 --> 01:08:27.163
- How're you doing?
- How're you?


01:08:27.173 --> 01:08:29.406
- What can I get you?
- A left hander, Charlie told me


01:08:29.415 --> 01:08:31.007
- about your nephew.
- Oh, Mr...


01:08:31.016 --> 01:08:33.449
- Yankees.
- Yeah, yeah! Hey, Steve!


01:08:33.459 --> 01:08:34.851
- Come here.
- Excuse me.


01:08:34.860 --> 01:08:37.894
He's good. Put him in the team.
You're good enough, right?


01:08:37.903 --> 01:08:40.135
I'm a Lucas.
Good enough on a bad day.


01:08:40.145 --> 01:08:44.340
So don't make it a bad day,
make it a good day, you understand?


01:08:44.350 --> 01:08:48.267
Excuse me. Police department.
Now back out, baby.


01:08:50.436 --> 01:08:52.148
I'll take your ass in, Jimmy.


01:08:52.158 --> 01:08:54.350
You can't take me in for that.


01:08:54.360 --> 01:08:56.833
I got a licence for that, motherfucker.


01:08:56.842 --> 01:09:00.759
You got a licence for this?
Excuse me, all right?


01:09:01.687 --> 01:09:03.607
Shit, all right!


01:09:04.370 --> 01:09:07.804
I got to arrest you.
Shit's too good to be on the street.


01:09:07.813 --> 01:09:10.526
- What you doin, man?
- You ain't arresting nobody.


01:09:10.536 --> 01:09:12.368
You bribing me now?


01:09:12.378 --> 01:09:16.092
I tell you what,
I'm arresting everybody. All of you.


01:09:16.102 --> 01:09:18.022
You first!


01:09:21.867 --> 01:09:24.260
- How can that be?
- What was that?


01:09:24.269 --> 01:09:26.382
Get this fuckin...
what's the matter with you?


01:09:26.392 --> 01:09:27.943
- What was that?
- What?


01:09:27.953 --> 01:09:33.094
- What the hell's wrong with you?
- What's your fuckin' problem?


01:09:35.681 --> 01:09:37.433
I just shot him in the leg.


01:09:37.442 --> 01:09:39.362
Damn, Jimmy!


01:09:40.005 --> 01:09:41.925
Get up!


01:09:54.380 --> 01:09:55.892
Everybody, get out!


01:09:55.901 --> 01:09:57.821
Get out!


01:09:58.183 --> 01:10:01.137
- Frank, it was an accident.
- Wasn't no goddamn accident.


01:10:01.147 --> 01:10:04.740
He don't feel shit cause he's coked up
all the motherfuckin' time!


01:10:04.750 --> 01:10:06.862
He's your driver,
get rid of him.


01:10:06.872 --> 01:10:08.183
He's your cousin!


01:10:08.193 --> 01:10:09.985
He ain't shit to me,
he means nothin'.


01:10:09.995 --> 01:10:12.508
- What'll he do, go back home?
- I don't give a damn!


01:10:12.518 --> 01:10:14.438
Send his ass home!


01:10:14.519 --> 01:10:16.672
Don't rub on that.
You'd block that.


01:10:16.681 --> 01:10:20.353
You understand?
That's alpaga, $25,000 alpaga.


01:10:20.405 --> 01:10:24.730
You'd block that shit.
Don't rub, put club soda on it.


01:10:25.411 --> 01:10:26.803
Listen, from now on,


01:10:26.812 --> 01:10:28.884
don't nobody talk to me directly,
understand?


01:10:28.893 --> 01:10:30.366
You got business with me,


01:10:30.376 --> 01:10:32.608
you talk to Huey,
Huey talks to me, got it?


01:10:32.617 --> 01:10:35.963
- All right.
- Never on the phone, got it?


01:10:36.101 --> 01:10:38.654
And take them
goddamn sunglasses off!


01:10:38.663 --> 01:10:42.662
- Take the goddamn sunglasses off!
- Damn it, man!


01:10:44.229 --> 01:10:46.841
Simple-minded ass motherfuckers.


01:11:01.166 --> 01:11:03.450
The whole place was imported


01:11:03.969 --> 01:11:05.889
brick by brick.


01:11:06.451 --> 01:11:08.371
Gloucestershire.


01:11:08.694 --> 01:11:10.614
- Who?
- Quite famous.


01:11:11.336 --> 01:11:13.256
Yours.


01:11:17.262 --> 01:11:19.182
Here you go.


01:11:23.148 --> 01:11:25.068
Pull!


01:11:29.514 --> 01:11:31.434
Come, Eva.


01:11:32.077 --> 01:11:36.157
I'm sure you're dying to see
the rest of the house.


01:11:38.443 --> 01:11:40.363
Of course. Excuse me.


01:11:42.047 --> 01:11:46.045
Thank you for a wonderful lunch.
It was delicious.


01:11:48.453 --> 01:11:51.064
What do you think of monopolies?


01:11:51.976 --> 01:11:54.530
- You mean, like the game?
- No, I just think


01:11:54.539 --> 01:11:56.812
monopolies are made illegal
in the country, Frank,


01:11:56.821 --> 01:11:58.934
cause no one wants to compete.


01:11:58.944 --> 01:12:02.017
Nobody wants to compete,
not with a monopoly.


01:12:02.026 --> 01:12:04.474
Let the dairy farmers do that,


01:12:04.710 --> 01:12:06.781
half of them'd
go out of business tomorrow.


01:12:06.791 --> 01:12:10.105
- I'm just trying to make a living.
- It's your right.


01:12:10.114 --> 01:12:12.726
Everybody's right. It's America.


01:12:12.877 --> 01:12:17.313
We just can't do it
at the unreasonable expense of others.


01:12:17.322 --> 01:12:19.314
Cause it becomes un-American.


01:12:19.324 --> 01:12:21.677
That's why the price we pay
for that gallon of milk


01:12:21.686 --> 01:12:23.518
never represents the true cost
of production


01:12:23.528 --> 01:12:26.401
cause it's gotta be controlled.
It's gotta be set.


01:12:26.410 --> 01:12:27.603
It's gotta be fair.


01:12:27.612 --> 01:12:30.045
Controlled by who?
I set a price I think is fair.


01:12:30.055 --> 01:12:31.687
- I don't think it is.
- You don't?


01:12:31.696 --> 01:12:32.808
I don't.


01:12:32.817 --> 01:12:35.010
I know your customers
are happy, Frank.


01:12:35.020 --> 01:12:37.692
Bunch of fuckin' junkies
that they are.


01:12:37.702 --> 01:12:40.721
What about your fellow dairy farmers?


01:12:40.745 --> 01:12:42.665
Are you thinking of us?


01:12:42.787 --> 01:12:44.620
You thinking of them?


01:12:44.629 --> 01:12:46.545
The dairy farmers?


01:12:46.555 --> 01:12:51.186
I'm thinking of them, Dominic, about
as much as they've thought about me.


01:12:51.196 --> 01:12:53.399
I'm just thinking out loud.


01:12:54.078 --> 01:12:56.671
If you took some of your inventory,


01:12:56.681 --> 01:12:58.803
and you sold it wholesale.


01:13:00.045 --> 01:13:02.727
Sit.
We could work.


01:13:03.568 --> 01:13:06.179
You could use some distribution.


01:13:06.531 --> 01:13:09.804
I dunno, I'm pretty good.
I got 110th to 155th,


01:13:09.814 --> 01:13:11.726
river to river, I'm all right.


01:13:11.736 --> 01:13:14.810
It's kind of a mom and pop store
next to what I'm talking about,


01:13:14.819 --> 01:13:16.531
and that's bigger than K-Mart.


01:13:16.540 --> 01:13:19.535
I'm talking about L.A.,
Chicago, Detroit, Las Vegas.


01:13:19.544 --> 01:13:21.464
Let's go nationwide.


01:13:21.546 --> 01:13:24.459
I'm gonna guarantee you
peace of mind here.


01:13:24.469 --> 01:13:26.389
You don't want that?


01:13:26.952 --> 01:13:28.872
You gonna need it.


01:13:29.033 --> 01:13:30.825
I don't know how you feel me.


01:13:30.835 --> 01:13:32.708
I'm kind of a Renaissance man.


01:13:32.717 --> 01:13:34.709
The people I deal with on a daily basis,


01:13:34.719 --> 01:13:36.674
they're not enlightened.


01:13:36.684 --> 01:13:39.193
You talk to them about civil rights,
they don't know.


01:13:39.203 --> 01:13:40.916
They're not open to change.


01:13:40.925 --> 01:13:44.520
Not from the way things are done,
and who's doing it.


01:13:44.529 --> 01:13:48.609
I can talk to them,
so there's no misunderstanding.


01:13:49.093 --> 01:13:51.949
That's what I mean
by peace of mind.


01:13:54.338 --> 01:13:56.258
Here


01:13:56.380 --> 01:13:59.807
You're paying what,
75, 80 thousand a kilo?


01:14:01.546 --> 01:14:03.668
I'm a Renaissance man too.


01:14:04.629 --> 01:14:06.549
I'd consider 50,000.


01:14:14.638 --> 01:14:17.912
Why would you trust these people?
And the way they look at you.


01:14:17.922 --> 01:14:20.315
They look at me like it's Xmas
and I'm Santa Claus.


01:14:20.324 --> 01:14:23.262
They look at us like we're the help.


01:14:23.488 --> 01:14:25.408
They work for me, now.


01:14:30.094 --> 01:14:32.326
<i>I predict it when I meet Joe Frazier,</i>


01:14:32.336 --> 01:14:34.529
<i>this will be like a good amateur</i>

